  "verdict": {
    "decision": "reject",
    "lever": "parallel prefill (local_max_concurrent_prefills > 1, i.e. the two-slot pool prefilling concurrently)",
    "measurement": "aggregate prefill throughput does not rise with concurrency: 156.1 tok/s at concurrency 2 vs 156.2 tok/s at concurrency 1 on the same 44,770-token prompt (ratio 1.00), while the wall window doubles (2.00x) and the slowest request in a round drops to 126.6 tok/s (0.81x).",
    "rollback_value": "the shipped serialised gate (local_max_concurrent_prefills: 1) keeps per-request first byte at the full single-stream rate; the lever would be re-enabled by setting the key to 0 (router_helpers._max_concurrent_prefills: 0 = cap disabled) with no code change, so a future adoption is a one-key config edit and its rollback the same."
  }
